//Multi-flag void method (AccessType NodeFlags KT_Void grammar variant):
//`public static void` requires the NodeFlags production — a single-flag
//rule alone would leave this shape a bare syntax error. 0.9.10 call-form
//namespaces: a static method is reachable only through the type name, so
//the call is written `Util.twice(...)`; the out param keeps the effect
//observable without touching instance state from a static method.
class Util {
	public static void twice(int v, out int r) {
		r = v * 2;
	}
}

int main() {
	int r = 0;
	Util.twice(21, out r);
	return r;
}
